   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Jobs",
     "texto": [
      "After **sunt** («I am»), the job usually goes without an article, unlike English, which needs «a»: **Sunt profesor** («I am a teacher»). Jobs with masculine and feminine forms agree with the person."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "To have",
     "texto": [
      "**A avea** means «to have». Its forms are **am, ai, are, avem, aveți, au**. In **am o profesie**, the article **o** goes with a feminine noun; **un** goes with a masculine one."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "The present tense of «a avea»",
